Dear Hiring Team,

It is with great pleasure that I submit my candidacy for the Software Engineer role with Lightfield. I bring over three years of professional experience building full-stack systems and production AI agents, along with a Master of Science in Computer Science from Pace University, NY.

At Sperse, I have owned full-stack product features for a multi-agent CRM from inception to impact, using TypeScript, React, Next.js, Node.js, Apollo GraphQL, Python, FastAPI, and PostgreSQL to route requests across 40+ specialized LLMs for more than 10,000 users. I also built a React Flow workflow platform with durable Temporal execution, a secure FastMCP server exposing 160+ backend actions, and production observability and metrics using OpenTelemetry, CloudWatch, and trace-based CI/CD evals. These systems required the same focus on reliability, scalability, performance, and exceptionally useful AI product experiences that Lightfield seeks. My OpenAI Codex and Bitbucket MCP review pipeline, which triages 25–30 pull requests each week and reduces reviewer load by hours, also reflects how I use code review and knowledge-sharing to strengthen engineering practices.

Previously at Qualitest, I built a cloud-agnostic Java and Spring Boot Storage Service backed by PostgreSQL and Redis, with secure file operations across Google Cloud Storage, S3, and MinIO. I improved scalability and performance through PostgreSQL window functions, materialized views, and indexes; communicated the resulting insights through interactive React visualizations; and used AWS Step Functions and Lambda to improve error recovery across 100K+ weekly executions. That experience prepared me to collaborate with product leaders, articulate technical decisions to technical and non-technical stakeholders, and independently deliver reliable systems in a fast-moving environment.

Lightfield's mission to help founders build better businesses through deep customer understanding resonates strongly with me. Its focus on building a world model that preserves customer context—and on agents that turn that context into reliable action—closely matches my work on multi-agent CRM orchestration, validated backend tools, and observable AI workflows. I would be excited to help create an intuitive, intelligent CRM that captures every interaction, compounds organizational knowledge, and gives teams the insight to build products customers love.

I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how I can contribute to Lightfield's product and technical vision. I can be reached at #ph or #eml. Thank you for your time and consideration; I look forward to connecting.

